1ST ASCENSION GAME SUMMARY ("The Frigid Wizard Goes to the Shopping Mall")

Dunamos the Mage          St:18 Dx:22 Co:16 In:25 Wi:25 Ch:18  Chaotic
Astral Plane $:0  HP:265(265) Pw:521(630) AC:-38 Xp:30/101539330 T:77048

This was only the second game I've gotten down to Medusa; for as long
as I've been playing nethack I could never get over the "hump" of the
early levels. Finally the lessons of the patient instructors in RGRN
are sinking in, and I'm playing more slowly and carefully. THANKS to
everyone for all you've taught me. This game was a lot of fun.

It might have turned out the same as many others; I did just escape from
being surrounded in the Mine's End room (a timely #pray'er). My other
brush with death was my "oLS saving me from a YASD (moved while blind
and felt a 'trice corpse). So I do still have a ways to go in learning
the craft. :-)

I actually got cone of cold and cold resistance very early on (even
earlier than magic missile) so that was what really got me through the
early game... that, and the two awesome stores on levels 8, 10.

After watching a Marvin game, I tried going invisible fairly early
on, and that made things a lot easier overall. This was also my first
experience with jumping boots and the haste-self spell, and I am hooked;
awesome combo. Also the first time I got teleportitis and ring of teleport
control working together.

I made heavy use of sped-up pets (notably dragons, gargoyles, unicorns,
and in late game, jabberwocks). Most of the time I had 3-6 and I think
next time I will not bother with all the work it takes to herd this many
of them at the stairways and portals, even with the whistle. 2 good ones
is probably enough.

I pretty much have the price-ID game down now; this time I had an
el-primo stash location (co-aligned altar was next door to the Sokoban
up-stairs). I am slowly learning to only take the essentials on each
mission, so I don't keep getting burdened and have to run back. Yes,
I am a pack-rat.

Ludios, the Castle, and water levels I found harder than I thought;
conversely, Gehennom seemed a lot easier than I thought. By the time my
AC was better than -30 and I had all the intrinsics, nothing was really
hurting me any more. Liches and teleporting demons take more work, but
are not dangerous once you learn their up-stairs trick. The most dangerous
thing in the game is the haste and inaccuracy of my own fingers. :-)

By the end of the game, I was in a strange position. I had lots of magic
marker charges and paper/spellbooks, my AC was already in great shape,
and I had all the spells I needed. It was hit points/experience level
that was clearly my weak spot. So I ended up using my last wishes for
potions of gain level, and I got one final succubus plus good drops
during the ascension, so I ended up with XL 30 HP 283 by the time I hit
astral. It seemed strange to be using wishes for this, but I feared the
HP 200 I had was not nearly enough for my first ascension.

